172,500,000

This estimate is derived from multiplying the estimated global giraffe population by the average number of spots per individual. Current conservation data estimates there are approximately 115,000 to 120,000 giraffes alive worldwide (combining wild and captive populations). Zoological and scientific sources generally cite an average of approximately 1,500 spots on an adult giraffe, which leads to the total calculation of 115,000 multiplied by 1,500.

